<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to publish sugar tax exemption Thursday.</title>
<headline>Brazil to publish sugar tax exemption Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government should publish on Thursday authorisation for exporters to start shipping sugars set aside in the government crop plan with a zero export tax, a top government official said.</p>
<p>&quot;(Industry and Commerce) Minister Francisco Dornelles and (Finance) Minister Pedro Malan have both signed the document. It should be published tomorrow,&quot; said Mauricio Assis, head of the Industry and Commerce Ministry's primary commodities department.</p>
<p>The publication of the notice is necessary to exempt exporters from a 40 percent export tax which otherwise applies to sugars exported in excess of the 5.39 million tonnes set out in crop plan published on April 30.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
